---
/**
 * Gene — first biology-lens concept (Single Identity scale).
 * Science-first reading of genetics: heritable founding configuration
 * passed to a new Identity. Explicitly not the full Identity Stem.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Gene | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Gene
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					The heritable founding configuration of an Identity:
					the inner image of self that can be passed to a new Identity
					so that continuity of lineage and independence of the new form can both hold.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: genetics as the discipline of heritable information across generations of living forms.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Gene is not the Identity Stem.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">What is passed, not what is lived.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, <strong class="text-white/85">genetics</strong> studies how living forms transmit heritable information
					to the next generation. A daughter cell receives DNA; from the moment of separation it is a
					<strong class="text-white/85">new</strong> living unit with its own membrane, metabolism, and further trajectory.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Gene</strong> names the same structural role under the biology lens:
					the <strong class="text-white/85">heritable founding configuration</strong> that one Identity can pass when a
					<strong class="text-white/85">new</strong> Identity begins.
				</p>
				<p>
					That includes human children, idea-identities, organizational spin-offs, and other offspring forms.
					Each starts with a founding core from a parent Identity, then develops its own Stem, vision, and trajectory.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Gene is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Heritable mass:</strong> the concentrated, passable core of how a form is founded,
						not the full surface of a life as it is currently lived.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Inner image of self that can be given away:</strong> a portable imprint of authorship origin,
						values-seed, and starting constraint, sufficient for a new Identity to begin recognizably related
						and still become other.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge between Identities:</strong> Gene is the biology-lens name for transmission
						<strong class="text-white/85">across</strong> Identity boundaries (parent → child, author → idea, form → spin-off).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Start of a new Stem, not the parent Stem:</strong> the new Identity receives Gene as founding input,
						then builds its own State Differential and Vision Gradient over time.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Gene is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Identity Stem.</strong>
						The Stem is the ongoing temporal object of <em class="text-white/75 not-italic">one</em> Identity:
						State Differential (past → present) and Vision Gradient (present → future) held in tension.
						Gene does not replace that. See <a href="/framework/time" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Time / Identity Stem</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the full trajectory of a life.</strong>
						Registry history, Geometry Receipts, and lived Mass belong to the Stem of the living form.
						Gene is only the passable founding slice, not the whole worldline.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not control of the offspring.</strong>
						Passing Gene does not keep Ownership over the new Identity.
						The child, idea, or spin-off becomes its own form with its own membrane and jurisdiction.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the agentic loop inside the form.</strong>
						Model weights, prompts, or tool harnesses may be part of what a runtime Identity transmits.
						They are machinery, not Gene as such. Identity is not the loop.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim that identity is DNA.</strong>
						Genetics supplies the science reading. The framework mapping is structural and operational,
						not a reduction of persons or ideas to molecular sequences.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Relation to Stem</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Founding core, not the living trunk.</h2>
				<p>
					An Identity may carry an <strong class="text-white/85">innermost core</strong> that persists across its own life:
					deep authorship orientation, non-negotiable constraints, the phase that still feels like "me"
					after large surface change. That core is part of how the Stem stays recognizable.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Gene</strong> is what can be extracted from that depth
					<strong class="text-white/85">as a founding gift to another Identity</strong>.
					It is related to the innermost core, but it is defined by transmissibility across a boundary,
					not by continuity inside one life.
				</p>
				<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/10">
					<table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-white/65">
						<thead class="border-b border-white/10 text-white/40">
							<tr>
								<th class="p-3 font-medium">Stem</th>
								<th class="p-3 font-medium">Gene</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10">
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3">One Identity over time</td>
								<td class="p-3">Transmission to a new Identity</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3">Lived worldline (State Differential + Vision Gradient)</td>
								<td class="p-3">Founding configuration at birth of the new form</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3">Ownership stays with the living form</td>
								<td class="p-3">Ownership is released with the gift</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3">Physics lens: Time</td>
								<td class="p-3">Biology lens: Genetics</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Name the founding gift:</strong> when you start a child Identity, an idea-identity, or a spin-off,
						what exactly is being passed, and what must stay yours?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Protect independence:</strong> Gene starts relatedness. It must not smuggle permanent control.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep Stem distinct:</strong> do not treat your full history as heritable payload.
						Pass a core, not a captivity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Honor lineage without identity collapse:</strong> the new form may carry your Gene and still owe you
						no obligation to remain a copy.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">genetics</strong> (heritable information across generations of living systems).
						Cell biology supplies the unit that receives Gene and then lives as its own form.
						Further biology-lens concepts (Cell, Metabolism, Signal, and others) will be founded separately.
						This page is the first explicit step of that lens, not the full map.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/time" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Time / Stem</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
